=[ Contributing to Ordiola ]

==[ Documentation Policy ]

-| All Markdown files (`README.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`, etc.) are generated build artifacts.
 | Never edit `.md` files directly.
-| Always edit the source `.tmt` files under @dir(tmtroot/).
-| Run `just docs` (or `tomet export .`) to regenerate Markdown files, and verify with `just docs-check`.

==[ Project Philosophy ]

Ordiola is a tool shaped by personal taste, not a product that aims to grow.

===[ Non-goals ]

- A marketplace or any other ecosystem for sharing plugins and themes.
- Hosted services such as a sync service. Git synchronization is provided by the Tomet ecosystem, and Ordiola only uses it.
- Migration tools or special handling for other applications' formats. Markdown files are treated like any other text file.
- Promotion, onboarding funnels, or comparisons that position Ordiola against other applications.

===[ Stability ]

Extension APIs and file formats may change without notice.
If you need a stable plugin API, Ordiola is not the right tool.

==[ Commit Convention ]

All commits must follow the Conventional Commits format: `type(scope): description`.

==[ Clean Commits Policy ]

Do not include AI session metadata or trailers in commit messages.
Keep commit logs clean and focused on technical changes.
